          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "قصبہ — qasbā — \"a small town\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ہمارا قصبہ شہر سے دور ہے۔ hamārā qasbā shahr se dūr hai. Our little town is a long way from the city."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Masculine."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "قصبہ (qasbā) is usually traced, through Persian, to Arabic qaṣaba, \"a chief town, a citadel\"; in Urdu it is a town smaller than a شہر."
            }
          ]
        },
